Taisei v1.4.6 Released!

This is a maintenance release that mostly consists of bug fixes and a few QoL improvements.

- **Use Vulkan by default on Windows**. Previous version used Direct3D 12 by default due to a change in the SDL library,
which didn't seem to work correctly for many Windows 10 users.

- **Windows version now asks to choose the rendering backend on startup**. This is necessary because we can't provide a
reliable default and fallback for this platform due to the state of its GPU drivers.

- **Fixed toggling fullscreen from the options menu** causing the game window to rapidly switch back and forth between
fullscreen and windowed modes.

- **Fixed some minor background rendering errors**, in particular in the non-OpenGL backends.

- **Fixed a crash** that occurred when attempting to enter the Stage Practice menu for a difficulty that the user has
never played before.

- **Fixed the binary releases not working** on some old CPUs that don't support AVX instructions.

- **The Switch homebrew build is back**.

- **Improved FPS limiter accuracy** on some systems.

- **Fixed "System" language option** always defaulting to English on some systems.

- **Implemented dialogue title cards for bosses**. Better late than never, I suppose.

- **Added options to adjust the background brightness, contrast, and saturation**.

- **Greatly improved visibility of Iku's cloud bullets** in Stage 5.

- **Minor localization improvements**. In particular, the French text now fits within the HUD layout.

- **Made saving progress and configuration more robust**, which should fix rare progress loss when saving is interrupted
(e.g. due to power loss or forced shutdown).


Grab the update from the [downloads section](/download).
